# Screens: the toolbar on the inventory screen. In VR the inventory shows the toolbar's slots along its bottom; a hand tool
# or gun dragged with the laser's trigger from your inventory onto slot 3 goes in slot 3, as the G menu puts it there.
# World: Earth Planet (survival, on foot). A pistol is given so the inventory surely holds a gun; slot 3 is emptied first.
# The plugin says, once the inventory page is shown, where the toolbar's slots and the first tool or gun you carry are
# on the panel; the right hand, before the face at 0.1 1.55 -0.2, points at each.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: a gun in the inventory and nothing in slot 3 -----------------------------------------------

give PhysicalGunObject/SemiAutoPistolItem
toolbar 3
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
expect headset steady
headset no-inventory.png
key I
wait 2
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
expect log Inventory toolbar: shown on the inventory page within 5

# ---- Where the inventory is drawn: standing in the world ahead, at the menu distance, and staying there ----------------

# A menu opens 2 m ahead of the head (Menu distance), level, at the height of the eyes, 60 degrees wide (Menu width),
# and stays where it opened while the head turns (Rendering/WorldMenu.cs).
headset inventory.png
expect headset new depth 1.5 2.6
expect headset new at 0 0 12
expect headset new size 35 75
head 0 1.6 0 20 0
wait 1
headset inventory-head-turned.png
expect headset new follows world
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
# Before: slot 3 is empty.
read toolbar
remember before items

# ---- Where the first tool or gun and slot 3 are ------------------------------------------------------------------------

remember tool log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, (\S+), at stage/' within 10
remember toolAt log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, .* the first tool or gun you carry, \S+, at stage \((\S+), (\S+), (\S+)\) m/' within 10
remember slot log '/Inventory toolbar: on the panel, its slots at stage .* 3 \((\S+), (\S+), (\S+)\), 4 /' within 10

# ---- The trigger on the tool, the hand turned to slot 3, the trigger let go ------------------------------------------

hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {toolAt}
wait 1
expect log Laser: pointing at the panel within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.3
# Turning past the hold that keeps a click from being a drag, then on to slot 3.
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {slot}
wait 0.5
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 toward {slot}
wait 0.5
release right trigger
wait 1
expect log /Inventory toolbar: .* put in slot 3/ within 5
read toolbar
expect items != {before}
expect items contains {tool}
expect no log Exception

key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
